}

### 5. Test with minimal data
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChildProfile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJodHRwOi8vd3d3LnczLm9yZy8yMDAxLzA0L3htbGRzaWctbW9yZSNobWFjLXNoYTI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..4ul0Pi9ZYg0JAgcUOGebFunoIVEIxCs5WhfJGwjnqDM

{
  "nickname": "Minimal Child",
  "ageInYears": 3,
  "ageInMonths": 0,
  "gender": 0,
  "supportNeedsLevel": 2
}

### 6. Test invalid data (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChildProfile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "nickname": "",
  "ageInYears": -1,
  "ageInMonths": 15,
  "gender": 99,
  "supportNeedsLevel": 10
}

### 7. Test without authorization (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChildProfile/GetProfile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### 8. Test with invalid token (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChildProfile/GetProfile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJodHRwOi8vd3d3LnczLm9yZy8yMDAxLzA0L3htbGRzaWctbW9yZSNobWFjLXNoYTI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..4ul0Pi9ZYg0JAgcUOGebFunoIVEIxCs5WhfJGwjnqDM

### Notes:
# Gender enum values (from Data.Entities.Enums.Gender):
# 0 = PreferNotToSay
# 1 = Male  
# 2 = Female

# SupportNeedsLevel enum values (from Data.Entities.Enums.SupportNeedsLevel):
# 0 = Low
# 1 = Medium
# 2 = High
# 3 = VeryHigh

# Replace YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE with an actual JWT token from authentication
# You can get this by logging in through your authentication endpoint
